{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>I am El Shaddai.</b> For I am sufficient to bless — for the blessings are Mine." "<b>Be fruitful and multiply.</b> Because Binyamin had not yet been born — and even though she had already conceived from him." "<b>A nation.</b> Binyamin." "<b>Nations.</b> Menasheh and Efrayim, who are destined to come forth from Yosef — and they are counted among the tribes (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>And kings.</b> Sha'ul and Ish-Boshet, who were from the tribe of Binyamin (Bereshit Rabbah), for they had not yet been born. And this verse Avner expounded when he made Ish-Boshet king, and the tribes too expounded it and drew Binyamin close, as it is written ״אִישׁ מִמֶּנּוּ לֹא יִתֵּן אֶת בִּתּוֹ לְבִנְיָמִין לְאִשָּׁה״ (Judges 21), and they went back and said: had one arisen from among the tribes, the Holy One, blessed be He, would not have said to Ya'akov ״וּמְלָכִים מֵחֲלָצֶיךָ יֵצֵאוּ״." "<b>A nation and a congregation of nations.</b> His sons are destined to become nations numbering like the nations — which are seventy peoples, and likewise every Sanhedrin is seventy. Another interpretation: his sons are destined to bring offerings even when the high places are forbidden, like the nations, in the days of Elijah."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:14.844217004Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}